concept :separation_leave do
  name "Separation Leave"
  tags :autonomy, :medicine, :surveillance, :symbiosis
  prominence :recognized

  prose <<~PROSE
    Seven days outside the #{ref :mycelial_neural_mesh, "neighbourhood network"}, available to an adult #{ref :the_joined, "Joined"} citizen who asks to make a decision without company. The request does not need a reason. A municipal symbiosis clinic may postpone the leave for an open wound, an immune crisis or another condition that requires continuous care; it cannot replace the request with counselling and call the matter settled.

    The clinic checks the citizen while their ordinary clothing can still report a baseline. A textile steward then cuts the mature #{ref :living_textiles, "garment"} at its living margins; #{ref :separation_film, "separation film"} keeps the two cut faces alive without letting them touch.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :operations, heading: "The Week"
    The citizen exchanges the garment for woven cellulose clothes and enters a disconnected clinic room. Morning and evening checks use glass thermometers, paper strips and spoken questions; no instrument inside can send a reading to the neighbourhood. #{ref :mulberry_court_clinic, "Mulberry Court Clinic"} keeps such rooms beside its ordinary connected wards.

    Staff keep the old garment alive beside the room. The citizen may end the leave at any check. Rejoining is treated as a completed leave rather than a failure: the steward unwraps the margins, seats them against the original sites and watches for inflammation while the garment takes hold.

    A citizen who remains for all seven days goes through the same graft and leaves after the first clean reading. The completion form records temperature, sleep, meals, inflammation, whether the garment took the graft, and any municipal action the citizen requests. It has no field for the decision itself. #{ref :the_fifth_room_week, "The Fifth-Room Week"} is one complete clinic record.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "What Care Continues"
    The #{ref :the_great_root, "Great Root"} classifies separation leave as planned interruption of care. The neighbourhood keeps the citizen's workplace, household duties and clinic appointments open; relatives may leave food or letters at the hatch and receive confirmation that the person has eaten, unless the citizen refuses that confirmation before the cut.

    A missed meal followed by a missed check brings a steward into the room with a disconnected medical kit. Declining to discuss the decision does not. The steward can end leave for an immediate danger to the citizen; the reason for the decision is not part of that assessment.
  PROSE
end
